 "verdict": "CONTROL: Pythia's seed-averaged diversity against diversity_multiseed's 8-seed means, in units of their measured across-seed sd: {128: 0.24, 256: 0.25, 512: 0.23, 1000: 0.33, 2000: 0.56, 4000: 0.53} sigma, worst 0.56 against a 2.5 gate. Agreement within seed noise, so the settle matches the geometry F111 was measured at. COHORT: cohort intact: all 3 declared familys measured PRIMARY: across-family spread of DIVERSITY at matched bits-per-byte is 55.5519 over 3 families, against 49.8712 at matched token count, with a seed floor of 2.8313. Diversity does NOT collapse against loss, mirroring lambda_ca's failure to (F100). Two quantities claimed to be functions of one another agree about whether model quality organises them, which is what F111 requires and what this test could have refuted. The reduction survives. BOUNDARY: three families, one radius, one temperature; bpb removes the tokenizer confound but not the corpus one, and architecture, data order and optimiser still differ across families simultaneously. bpb and lambda were re-used unchanged, so only diversity is new.",
